§§ `14.5 — How a payment is applied`

-- src:1480 | 14.5 Phương thức phân bổ phí bảo hiểm:

-- Shared by both periods: what is left of a payment once the basic and rider premiums due
-- are paid becomes accumulation premium only if the contract year's premiums are then paid in
-- full (14.5.1(iv), 14.5.2(iii)). Where they are not, 14.5 does not say where the excess goes;
-- and 1.16 caps accumulation premium without saying what becomes of an excess over the cap.
-- Both are declined (finding FD22).
@ref V082021 14.5.1(iv), 14.5.2(iii) and 1.16
GIVEN `the excess` IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `The contract`
      p IS A `A premium payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`14.5 — the accumulation premium made of an excess of` `the excess` `under` c `:` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the excess` EQUALS 0
        THEN 0
        IF   p's `basic and rider premiums of the contract year still to fall due after this one` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN REFUSE "14.5 does not say what becomes of a payment above the instalment due before the contract year's premiums are paid in full"
        IF   p's `accumulation premiums already received in the contract year` PLUS `the excess`
                 GREATER THAN `1.16 — the most accumulation premium the contract may take in one contract year` c
        THEN REFUSE "1.16 caps the accumulation premium of a contract year and does not say what becomes of a payment above the cap"
        OTHERWISE `the excess`

